invariant: INV-5
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_test
reason: the key call skips the line breaks after an EC PARAMETERS block
  and does not require them to end in LF, so the key's BEGIN line may
  follow the END line on the same line, or after a lone CR, which ends no
  line. The ruling keeps a key file strict (docs/decisions.md 131).
  test_key_parameters writes both and requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
           x509_pem_parameters_are_p256(parameters, w.len) && pem_skip_line_breaks(r) == '\n';
--- new
           x509_pem_parameters_are_p256(parameters, w.len) && (pem_skip_line_breaks(r), 1);
